      trivia: "Pepín Rodríguez, who took control in 1903, was a publicity genius who raced his beloved horse “Julieta” at courses around the world and had 20,000 varieties of personalised bands made for wealthy clients. The name of one client, Winston Churchill, has become part of the cigar world’s common tongue as the name of the 7 × 47 vitola. The first Dominican Romeo was rolled at the Quesada family’s MATASA factory (1978), and in the 150th-anniversary year of 2025 a commemorative humidor named the “Palazzo of Love” (containing the limited vitola “Reconciliation”, 6½ × 52) was put up at Procigar’s charity auction."
