      trivia: "The brand name was born of a surname people misread. Michael Chiusano, who brought home about a hundred bandless cigars he had taken to on a Dominican trip, cut up his firm’s letterhead to make improvised bands — and, advised that most people would mispronounce the printed spelling Chiusano, changed it to the phonetic Cusano. Davidoff, moreover, had been contract-manufacturing Cusano since before the acquisition — the cigars were rolled at Hendrik Kelner’s factory — but held no stake; with the purchase of 2009 the maker at last became the owner. The founder Michael returned to the trade in 2013, the year after his non-compete agreement lapsed, with the new marque Loose Cannon"
